(7133028, 1087960, 93565, '<td valign="top">Being that these are a plague (literally, they carry the plague out here) upon the land, I''m amazed to see one get top honors here. Not going to lie- something I''d never thought I''d see.<br/>Well shot.<br/>And as to their foliage eating- they do this with pretty much everything, picking up all manner of things and chomping upon it.  The ones in more urban areas are EXTREMELY tame, to the extent that you could get close enough to achieve your FoV with a 50mm, but in the boonies, you''d need at least a 500mm lens. Strange little creatures.<br/> <br/>Did they do all the same noises at the zoo? I can''t imagine you got to hear all of them, as the tame ones are much less interesting in that regard.</td>', 'Being that these are a plague (literally, they carry the plague out here) upon the land, I''m amazed to see one get top honors here. Not going to lie- something I''d never thought I''d see.Well shot.And as to their foliage eating- they do this with pretty much everything, picking up all manner of things and chomping upon it.  The ones in more urban areas are EXTREMELY tame, to the extent that you could get close enough to achieve your FoV with a 50mm, but in the boonies, you''d need at least a 500mm lens. Strange little creatures. Did they do all the same noises at the zoo? I can''t imagine you got to hear all of them, as the tame ones are much less interesting in that regard.', '2013-11-21 01:15:23.000000', NULL, 0),
